  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Ziziphus mauritiana",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziziphus_mauritiana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1376086249,
      "text": "Ziziphus mauritiana, also known as Indian jujube, Indian plum, Chinese apple, ber and dunks, is a tropical, spiny, evergreen shrub or small tree in the buckthorn family Rhamnaceae. It is often confused with the closely related Chinese jujube : Z. mauritiana is common in tropical and subtropical climates, while Z. jujuba prefers temperate climates."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Ziziphus mauritiana",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziziphus_mauritiana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175248325,
      "text": "Ziziphus mauritiana también conocida como ponsigué (Venezuela), badari (sánscrito), Kul (bengalí), Ber (hindi), Dongs, Boroi, Bor, Beri, Bidara, ciruela india, Jojoba india o Jujube mauritiano es una especie de árbol frutal tropical, perteneciente a la familia Rhamnaceae."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Ziziphus mauritiana",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziziphus_mauritiana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 236113365,
      "text": "Ziziphus mauritiana, le Jujubier de Maurice, ou Surettier et Pomme surette aux Antilles, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Rhamnaceae. C'est un arbre qui pousse principalement dans les régions tropicales sèches et qui est utilisé comme nourriture animale, comme médicament, comme combustible et comme aliment."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Ziziphus mauritiana",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziziphus_mauritiana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 72196958,
      "text": "Ziziphus mauritiana, também conhecida como jujuba indiana, ameixa indiana, maçã chinesa, ber e bora, é uma árvore tropical, espinhosa e perene da família Rhamnaceae. É frequentemente confundida com a jujuba chinesa, espécie intimamente relacionada. Z. mauritiana é comum em climas tropicais e subtropicais, enquanto Z. jujuba prefere climas temperados."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Bidara",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bidara",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29799569,
      "text": "Bidara atau widara adalah sejenis pohon kecil penghasil buah yang tumbuh di daerah kering. Tanaman ini dikenal pula dengan berbagai nama daerah seperti widara atau dipendekkan menjadi dara (Jw.); bukkol (Md.); bĕkul (Bal.); gol (Sas.); ko (Sawu); kok (Rote); kom, kon ; bĕdara (Alor); bidara (Makassar); rangga ; serta kalangga."
    }
  },
